# A CRLF Haml template's blank line is the single byte `\r`, which the
# reader counted as a line at the left margin: it ended the `do` block
# before it, so the block's parameter after the blank (4:5) read as a
# helper call; it ended a `-#` comment, so the comment's body was read as
# Ruby and credited `noted` with a call; and it ended a `:ruby` filter, so
# the filter's next line was text and `two` lost its call.
